# evidence-volatile: \d+\.\d+s
# evidence-volatile: Installed \d+ packages in \d+ms
#
# D-101 + D-104 — the directive channel gets a real grammar, as one thing.
# Both defects are the same root cause: directive text was trusted end to end.
#
# D-101: the override was a SUBSTRING test followed by `return scoped or {"*"}`,
# so any mention de-escalated every class. A directive FORBIDDING the override
# therefore disabled escalation wholesale — semantics exactly inverted from
# operator intent, with no signal. The first table is that inversion, and the
# second half is the capability the narrowing must not remove.
#
# D-104: `_read_directives` splits on line-prefix markers, and
# `foundry_inject_directive` neither escaped nor rejected them, so a
# priority="normal" body carrying a `### [URGENT]` line came back out as a
# SECOND, urgent directive. Read the composed row: `urgent=1 normal=1
# override=ALL` is one normal-priority call forging urgency AND smuggling a
# wholesale escalation override in a single shot.
#
# The indented row is refused slightly conservatively: it is inert under the
# parser TODAY (which keys on str.startswith), but a body smuggling one is
# asking for exactly that reading, and the cost of declining it is a rephrase.
